## Overview

Hlabeard Productions, in collaboration with the SATO48 Film Challenge, presents "FiveFest"—a dynamic festival dedicated to celebrating the art of short films with a maximum length of five minutes.

## Submission Guidelines

### 1. Film Duration and Content

Films must be exactly 5 minutes or less in length including credits. You are not allowed to upload a file that is longer than 5 minutes in duration.

Non-English dialogue films must include English subtitles or be dubbed in English.

Do not upload works in progress. Uploaded films must be complete and theater-projection ready.

The film's genre must be one of the following: Animation, Comedy, Documentary, Drama, Experimental, Horror, Music Video, Musical.

### 2. Technical Requirements

The minimum resolution is 720p.

Submitted films must have clear audio quality.

A film Poster and any other Promotional Materials are encouraged (though not required) to be uploaded.

### 3. Eligibility

Open to all filmmakers, regardless of age, region, production date of film, or content within specified genres.

### 4. Submission Process

FilmFreeway.

## Judging and Awards

### 5. Judging Panel

A select group of industry professionals and esteemed members of the filmmaking community will judge the entries.

Registered team members from last year's SATO48-Challenge are automatically opted IN and therefore may participate as Academy Judges if they so elect.

### 6. Prizes

- Best Animation
- Best Comedy
- Best Documentary
- Best Drama
- Best Experimental Film
- Best Horror
- Best Music Video
- Best Musical

## Venue and Event Details

### 7. Festival Locations (depending on needed capacity)

Alamo Drafthouse Cinema, Springfield, Missouri (The largest Alamo Drafthouse Cinema in the United States)

### 8. FiveFest Programming

All films are accepted into FiveFest, as follows:

Accepted films will receive a FiveFest Scorecard detailing, in the aggregate, how the Academy Judges responded to their film and an exclusive month-long online screening.

Some films will be selected for (a) an in-theater screening at a Festival Location, and (b) acknowledged as a Nominee at October FiveFest Awards Ceremony.

The winning film in each genre — for whom a representative of the film is present and checked in at the October FiveFest Awards Ceremony — receives the following:

- Statuette
- On-stage acceptance speech opportunity
- Backstage interview

### 9. Notification of Your Acceptance Level

You are notified via email of your film's Acceptance Level.

### 10. FiveFest Dates To Save

The submission closing date - September 1, 2026

In-theater screening, if applicable to your film, takes place at a date/time to be determined by capacity of Festival Locations.

October FiveFest Awards Ceremony - Exact Date TBD, 2nd Week of October

Online viewing, applicable to all films, takes place - TBD

## Legal Terms and Conditions

### 11. Film Rights

Entrant must own all rights to their film and its content.

All Entrants grant Hlabeard Productions and SATO48 the following:

In-theater screening and paywall online usage rights for the duration of SATO48-2024 FiveFest.

Free online usage rights within Festival Manager and promotional usage rights in perpetuity.

Entrant holds Hlabeard Productions, SATO48, and all other parties connected to SATO48, harmless in all respects.

### 12. Endorsement

Participation in FiveFest by Entrant is not an endorsement by Hlabeard Productions, nor SATO48, of the film's content.

### 13. Liability

Hlabeard Productions and SATO48 are not liable for any losses or damages incurred for any reason by Entrant.

### 14. Cancellation & Delays

In case of unavoidable cancellations or delays, efforts will be made to reschedule. No liability by Hlabeard Productions nor SATO48 is assumed for losses incurred due to such cancellations.

## Accessibility and Inclusion

### 15. Accessibility

FiveFest venues are wheelchair accessible.

### 16. Inclusion

FiveFest is committed to diversity and inclusion.

